{"nodes": [{"id": "security_seguridad_optimizador_pc", "label": "Seguridad \u2014 Optimizador PC (SECURITY.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L1-35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Audit reference: threat model, registry write contract, attack surface, test-enforced invariants, accepted/pending risks. Reviewed 2026-09-06, 2026-09-07 and 2026-11-08 (new Cleanup/Power commands, FolderCleanup deletion, guides)."}, {"id": "security_threat_model", "label": "Threat model (elevated, no console, portable, unsigned)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L37-56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ps2exe -requireAdmin -noConsole single-file exe without Authenticode. Real risks by severity: 1) leaving the PC less secure (UAC/Defender/SmartScreen/firewall/Update off), 2) leaving it broken without rollback, 3) running foreign code as admin."}, {"id": "security_attack_surface", "label": "Attack surface (no network, repo-authored inputs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L60-83", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only external inputs: settings.json (parsed defensively), the registry read (Registry64, never throws), repo-authored links/values/command steps, command output (displayed only) and guides (text only). No Invoke-Expression, scriptblock::Create, runtime Add-Type or downloads."}, {"id": "security_registry_write_contract", "label": "Registry write contract (Writer.ps1 / SettingApply.ps1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L87-93", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only Writer.ps1 writes (one key per call), triggered by SettingApply.ps1 toggles. 47 settings with -Registry, all in the Regedit section, one setting per key; NetworkThrottlingIndex was the first wired (benign, reversible)."}, {"id": "security_registry_write_allowlist", "label": "$RegistryWriteAllowlist / $RegistryWriteAllowedValues", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L95-130", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No denylist: what is not listed is blocked. Prefixes: Multimedia SystemProfile, HKLM/HKCU Software Policies Microsoft, Control Panel Desktop/Mouse, test branch. Value-by-value list admits 7 service Start values, 4 Tcpip Parameters values (not Interfaces), 6 LanmanServer values, DisableWpbtExecution, EnablePrefetcher, HibernateEnabled and BF6 privacy values. Known Medium risk: Policies Microsoft prefix reaches Defender/Update/SmartScreen GPO keys."}, {"id": "security_five_write_conditions", "label": "Five conditions of each registry write", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L132-153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documented Default for restore; distinguish missing vs other value (pending: revert of non-existing value should delete); path validated against allowlist with Registry64; declared type respected (typemismatch, MultiString unsupported); never touch ACLs/owners. Plus snapshot, read-back verification and -WhatIf."}, {"id": "security_write_result_states", "label": "Write-RegistryValue result states", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L155-172", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "written, nochange, blocked, badpath, typefail, unsupported, typemismatch, denied, disarmed; each attempt logs write attempt / post write / result blocks."}, {"id": "security_security_degrading_denylist", "label": "Security-degrading value-name denylist + AllowsSecurityTradeoff", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L174-201", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lowering security is allowed only if not Recommended, described, off by default and flagged AllowsSecurityTradeoff = $true. Names include EnableLUA, DisableAntiSpyware, SmartScreenEnabled, NoAutoUpdate, NoAutoRebootWithLoggedOnUsers, EnableFirewall. Mirrors $peligrosos in Security.Tests.ps1; zero settings touch it today."}, {"id": "security_rollback_snapshots", "label": "$RegistrySnapshots in-memory rollback", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L205-219", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hard contract is each key's Default; snapshot keeps prior value/type/existence. Lives only in memory: no undo UI, no restore-point warning. Pending: persist to %APPDATA%, undo button, restore-point notice."}, {"id": "security_code_execution_prohibitions", "label": "Code execution hard prohibitions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L223-240", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Running as admin: no iex/scriptblock::Create, no runtime Add-Type, no web cmdlets, no unquoted Start-Process, process start only in CommandRunner/ExternalLink, deletion only in FolderCleanup, no interpreters, nothing from world-writable folders, no -ExecutionPolicy Bypass in product."}, {"id": "security_external_link", "label": "ExternalLink http/https only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L244-256", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ShellExecute from an elevated process would open anything, so $ExternalLinkSchemes is exactly http/https, absolute URI required, pure test function, disallowed schemes never reach Start-Process."}, {"id": "security_user_data_log", "label": "User data and activity log export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L260-279", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "settings.json holds only UI preferences. The log can be exported by user action; cleanup detail (user file paths, recycle bin names) is written only with the 'Con detalle' checkbox. No telemetry, no outbound network."}, {"id": "security_supply_chain", "label": "Supply chain: ps2exe pinned 1.0.18, unsigned exe, Semgrep CI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L283-308", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ps2exe pinned by -RequiredVersion and PSGallery so each build uses the same compiler; unsigned exe blocks third-party distribution (EV cert suggested); checkout action pinned by SHA."}, {"id": "security_static_analysis", "label": "Static analysis (PSScriptAnalyzer, Semgrep; Snyk rejected)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L312-376", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PSSA: 0 errors, 2 false positives (dot-sourced vars); strict core pass: only verb warnings, Write-RegistryValue has ShouldProcess. Snyk rejected: no dependency manifests, pure PowerShell; Gitleaks, Authenticode and UIA smoke test suggested instead."}, {"id": "security_semgrep", "label": "Semgrep", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L342-358", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "semgrep ci in container; p/powershell no longer exists so PowerShell coverage is limited; one finding (mutable action tag) fixed. Pending: SARIF upload, versioned --config."}, {"id": "security_security_tests_invariants", "label": "Security invariants (tests/Source/Security.Tests.ps1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L380-410", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turns prose rules into failing tests: allowlisted -Registry paths, no dynamic exec/network, denylist flag, http/https only, single process/deletion doors, cleanup folders inside profile, recycle bin and advfirewall steps unchecked with warning, allowlists without interpreters or security services."}, {"id": "security_accepted_risks", "label": "Accepted and pending risks table", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L414-426", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "security_command_execution_contract", "label": "Command execution contract (CommandRunner.ps1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L430-495", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Internet/Cleanup/Power sections run Windows programs: no shell (UseShellExecute false), executables by name only resolved from System folder ($CommandAllowedExecutables), literal repo arguments, only Dhcp/Dnscache started ($CommandAllowedServices), file order not click order, nothing throws, logged, disarmable. Adding an exe/service/folder is a security decision."}, {"id": "security_folder_cleanup_contract", "label": "FolderCleanup.ps1 sole deletion gate ($CleanupAllowedFolders)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L459-479", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deleting from an elevated process is irreversible, so one place with a folder allowlist: only %TEMP%/%LOCALAPPDATA%/%APPDATA%, always inside the user profile, links never followed, folders emptied not removed, in-use files skipped, 80 ms chunks; recycle bin via Clear-RecycleBin, never pre-checked. Replaces the .cmd del /q."}, {"id": "security_skipif_registry_read", "label": "-SkipIf read-only registry check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L497-500", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A step may declare a registry value; if present the step ends succeeded ('already in place'). Exists because powercfg returns the same code for 'already exists' as for any failure. Read only, after the disarm check."}, {"id": "security_powercfg_fixed_guid", "label": "Power section: powercfg Ultimate Performance at fixed GUID", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L493-495", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only /duplicatescheme of the hidden Ultimate Performance template to a fixed program GUID and /setactive of it; never deletes or edits other plans."}, {"id": "security_guides_display_only", "label": "Guides shown as text only (Base64 in exe, never executed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L32-33, L76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guide .md files are embedded as Base64, parsed by Markdown.ps1 into a read-only RichTextBox and never executed; their links pass through Invoke-ExternalLink."}, {"id": "security_add_type_interop", "label": "Add-Type literal C# in SystemBackdrop.ps1 and WorkArea.ps1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L78-83, L423", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted: fixed reviewed literal strings; WorkArea subclasses only its own window for WM_GETMINMAXINFO."}], "edges": [{"source": "security_seguridad_optimizador_pc", "target": "readme_optimizador_pc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "SECURITY.md", "source_location": "L7-9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "security_seguridad_optimiza